    <div class="history-card">
      <div class="history-inner">
        <div class="history-year">1969</div>
        <div class="history-text">
          The original Lunar Lander was written by <strong>Jim Storer</strong>, a high school student, on a <strong>DEC PDP-8</strong> in a language called FOCAL. It fit on a single page. David Ahl later ported it to BASIC and published it in <em>101 BASIC Computer Games</em> (1973). By the end of the decade, every computer owner had played some version of it.
          <br><br>
          We're building that same game — the real one, with the real physics — in Python, in 2026.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── THE SITUATION ── -->
